  "generated_text": "1. The ball is initially dropped from a height of 16 meters.\n2. On the first bounce, it rises to a height of \\(\\frac{3}{4} \\times 16 = 12\\) meters.\n3. On the second bounce, it rises to a height of \\(\\frac{3}{4} \\times 12 = 9\\) meters.\n\nNow, let's calculate the total distance traveled:\n\n- Initial drop: 16 meters\n- First bounce: 12 meters\n- Second bounce: 9 meters\n\nAdding these distances together:\n\\[ 16 + 12 + 9 = 37 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nSo, the ball has traveled \\(\\boxed{37}\\) meters.",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[37, '37']",
    "gold_answer": "The ball traveled $16+16\\cdot\\frac34+16\\cdot\\left(\\frac34\\right)^2 = 16+ 12+9 = 37$ meters on its three descents. The ball also traveled $16\\cdot\\frac34+16\\cdot\\left(\\frac34\\right)^2+16\\cdot\\left(\\frac34\\right)^3 = 12+9+\\frac{27}4 = 27.75$ meters on its three ascents. Thus, the ball traveled $37+27.75 = 64.75 \\approx \\boxed{65}$ meters total.",
    "is_correct": false
  },
